# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# App
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is what ticket links and QR codes are built from, so in
# production it must be the real origin. If unset it falls back to
# https://tsakanisessions.co.za (see lib/seo.ts), never to a relative path — a
# relative URL would be a dead link in every mail client and an unscannable QR.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=Tsakani Sessions

# WhatsApp
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=27769961477

# Email — REQUIRED for ticket confirmations (resend.com)
#
# Never put the real key in this file. .env.example is committed; put live values
# in .env.local (gitignored) and in the Vercel project settings.
#
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the app still takes orders and still shows the buyer
# their order number and QR on screen, but no confirmation email is sent — and
# the email is the thing they keep. Set it.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL must be on a domain you have verified at resend.com/domains.
# Sending from an unverified domain fails with a 403 on every order, so this is
# not a cosmetic setting. Until a domain is verified the ONLY address that works
# is Resend's shared sandbox, onboarding@resend.dev, which delivers unreliably
# and often lands in spam:
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Tsakani Sessions <onboarding@resend.dev>
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Tsakani Sessions <hello@yourdomain.co.za>
#
# Where the "new order" alerts go. Falls back to tsakanisessions@gmail.com.
ADMIN_EMAIL=you@yourdomain.co.za
#
# Where a buyer's REPLY lands. The sending domain has no MX record (Resend's
# "Enable Receiving" is deliberately off, since it would claim the root MX and
# block ever putting real mailboxes on the domain), so without this a reply to a
# ticket confirmation bounces. Must be an inbox someone actually reads.
# Falls back to ADMIN_EMAIL.
REPLY_TO_EMAIL=you@yourdomain.co.za

# Analytics
# First-party analytics is built in (no third-party scripts). It writes to the
# analytics_events table via /api/track and is read by /admin/analytics.
# Set to "true" to disable all client-side tracking (e.g. for staging).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DISABLED=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Breazy Analytics — the SECOND analytics pipeline, /api/e and public/bz.js.
#
# It runs alongside /api/track above, it does not replace it. The one above
# knows the product (which event, which tee, which booking form). This one knows
# the visit, and knows it across every site Brendon runs, which the one above
# cannot see. Removing either loses something. See app/api/e/route.ts.
#
# NOTHING IS COLLECTED UNTIL ALL THREE OF BZ_SITE, BZ_SALT AND BZ_INGEST_SECRET
# ARE SET. The collect route checks for them first and returns 204 without
# reading the body, so an unconfigured deploy is inert rather than broken. That
# means a deploy of this branch changes nothing on its own.
#
# The site name inside the analytics service. Must be exactly "tsakani", which
# is what public/bz.js sends as data-site and what the dashboard groups on.
BZ_SITE=tsakani
#
# Per-site secret used to derive the daily counting value, an HMAC over site,
# day, IP and user agent. The IP is never stored, only hashed into this.
#
# THIS SALT MUST BE UNIQUE TO THIS SITE. POPIA section 57 requires prior
# authorisation from the Information Regulator before a unique identifier is
# processed across separate responsible parties to link them. A shared salt
# would make the same visitor produce the same value on two different sites,
# which is exactly that. A per-site salt makes the two values unrelated, so the
# unlinkability is a property of the arithmetic rather than a promise. Generate
# a fresh random value, never copy one from another site.
BZ_SALT=
#
# Shared secret the central analytics Worker checks on ingest. Same value across
# sites, it authenticates the server-to-server forward. Never sent to a browser.
BZ_INGEST_SECRET=
#
# Where the collect route forwards to. Optional; defaults to the live Worker.
# BZ_ENDPOINT=https://breazy-analytics.breazy.workers.dev/e
#
# Optional. Set to "off" to stop recognising returning visitors entirely: no
# _bza cookie is read or written and nothing is stored on the device. That
# switch exists for UK sites, where the statistical purposes exception covers
# how a service is used but not who uses it. This is a South African site under
# POPIA, which has no cookie rule at all, so it stays on here.
# BZ_RETURNING=off
